card.statement:
Let $\mathfrak{g}, \mathfrak{g}^{\theta}$ be a symmetric pair of type AIII/AIV such that $r = \lfloor (n+1)/2\rfloor$. Let $\Gamma_{\theta} = \{\beta_1, \dots, \beta_r\}$ where $\beta_j = \alpha_j + \alpha_{j+1} + \cdots + \alpha_{n-j+1}$ and set $\alpha_{\beta_j} = \alpha_j$ for each $j$. Then

\begin{align}
\mathcal{H} = \mathbb{C}[\mathcal{T}_{\theta}][H_1', \dots, H_r']
\end{align}

where $\mathcal{H}$ is the quantum Cartan subalgebra as defined in Theorem <<ref:theorem:main>> and

\begin{align*}
H_j' = [B_{n-j+1}, [B_{n-j}, \dots, [B_{j+1}, B_j]_q]_q\cdots]_q
\end{align*}

for all $j=1, \dots, r$.
